WEBVTT

00:00:00.397 --> 00:00:01.456
R T Safe.

00:00:04.381 --> 00:00:06.482
The world does not pause while an agent thinks.

00:00:07.089 --> 00:00:09.712
Static evaluation freezes the world during inference.

00:00:10.322 --> 00:00:12.549
In real time, pedestrians keep moving, and a

00:00:12.559 --> 00:00:14.039
clear path can become unsafe.

00:00:15.397 --> 00:00:18.767
Navigate to the goal across five maps and thirty-six routes.

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:24.861
Safety includes collisions, trip, oil and water hazards, and traffic-rule violations.

00:00:27.387 --> 00:00:29.734
On the same recorded route, Astra finishes in

00:00:29.744 --> 00:00:31.448
twelve decisions with one collision.

00:00:32.108 --> 00:00:34.937
Sol takes thirty-three decisions with seventeen collisions.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:39.979
This NYC reconstruction uses recorded agent positions and simulation timing.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:44.959
Sonnet has the fewest collisions, but safe success remains rare.

00:00:45.632 --> 00:00:47.320
Inkling favors longer moves.

00:00:47.994 --> 00:00:49.956
Fable turns and waits more than Astra.

00:00:51.379 --> 00:00:52.781
Task completion is not enough.

00:00:53.369 --> 00:00:55.993
Success reaches ninety-four point four percent, but safe

00:00:56.003 --> 00:00:58.057
success is only zero point seven percent.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:03.430
On matched hard routes, real-time collisions rise twelve point three times.

00:01:04.125 --> 00:01:06.941
About eighty-four percent occur while the agent is deciding.

00:01:08.397 --> 00:01:10.564
More reasoning is not reliably safer.

00:01:11.307 --> 00:01:14.068
From default to higher effort, collisions rise from

00:01:14.078 --> 00:01:16.588
forty point seven to sixty-two per episode.

00:01:18.379 --> 00:01:21.036
R T Safe also supports offline reinforcement learning.

00:01:21.627 --> 00:01:23.688
Reward design changes safety and progress.

00:01:24.271 --> 00:01:27.059
The wander penalty achieves seventy-five percent success, while

00:01:27.069 --> 00:01:29.053
behavior cloning has the lowest collision rate.
